Z||000000||Pheagey||10-10-2001||07:35 AM||||   I attempted to install my blacklight and to no avale. I'd like some input on how one wires in an extrs light to a '88 coupe. Thanks<BR> <A HREF="http://www.lithiumEffects.com/car.html" TARGET=_blank>www.lithiumEffects.com/car.html</A> <BR>Pheagey's Fiero site comming soon!||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-10-2001||02:20 PM||||I assume it just has a +12V wire and then a ground, usually denoted by the black and red wires.  Connect the black wire to a good ground (frame of car, make sure it touches metal), and then connect the red wire to your switch.  Run the other wire from the switch to the fusebox, crimp on a male terminal, and plug it into one of the empty ports in the fusebox labeled "IGN".  These connections are hot when the car is turned on.||||reg||1
